Package: mouthtype-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: CodesWhat <80784472+scttbnsn@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, curl, pipewire-audio, wl-clipboard, wtype, libnotify-bin, ffmpeg
Recommends: hyprland, libgomp1
Suggests: quickshell
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://mouthtype.app/linux/
Description: local voice dictation client for Wayland desktops
 Mouthtype records on a hotkey, transcribes on this machine with a pinned
 speech model and delivers the text to the focused window. Nothing leaves the
 computer.
 .
 This package installs the client, the Omarchy bar plugin sources and two
 systemd user units. The first-run unit is enabled for every user: at the next
 login it downloads the pinned speech model (about 465 MiB), sets up the bar
 widget and shortcuts, and enables the per-user service, reporting progress
 and any failure as notifications. Run "mouthtype-linux-setup" as your normal
 user to repeat or repair that by hand.
 .
 Development client for Linux x86_64. Paste and type delivery use Hyprland
 (recommended). The bar plugin needs Quickshell, which Debian and Ubuntu do
 not package, so it is only listed as a suggestion.
